 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-- **Normalization:** If the sum of weights is zero or near-zero, division by zero occurs. Guard against this [S1, unofficial].
-- **Boundary Conditions:** The neighborhood $\mathbf{x}'$ may fall outside the image bounds. Standard convolution handles this via padding; spatially varying kernels require explicit handling (e.g., clamping, mirroring, or ignoring out-of-bounds contributions) [S1, unofficial].
-- **Complexity:** The naive implementation is $O(n^2 m^2)$, where $m$ is the kernel radius. FFT cannot be used [S1, unofficial].
